COMMITTEE ACTION: On 2027-10-26 the Senate Commerce Committee ordered S. 1147, the National AI Standards and Competitiveness Act, reported favorably by voice vote (Committee Print 120-22, issued 2027-10-27, effective 2027-10-27).

Key adopted provisions:
(1) One national standard for frontier AI disclosure and evaluation, preempting inconsistent state requirements;
(2) Codification of voluntary pre-deployment commitments already in industry practice, without a new federal licensure regime;
(3) A competitiveness review so that any future rulemaking is measured against the EU high-risk timeline and the China CAC regime;
(4) A single reporting portal to end duplicative filings.

The Committee will not create a new approval bureaucracy on top of commitments industry has already made. Full text and the section-by-section are posted to the Committee site.

